       NMDOJ’S MOTION TO FILE A STATEMENT OF POSITION IN LIEU OF
                       TESTIMONY OUT OF TIME

       COMES NOW the New Mexico Department of Justice (NMDOJ) pursuant to 1.2.2.12

NMAC and requests the Commission to allow it to file its Statement of Position in Lieu of

Testimony Out of Time. In support of this Motion, NMDOJ states as follows:

       1.      NMDOJ missed the filing deadline as a consequence of excusable neglect based, in

part, on an inadvertent misunderstanding of its responsibilities and a family medical issue affecting

one of NMDOJ’s attorneys.

       2.      No party would be prejudiced by the granting of this Motion.

       3.      The positions of the parties are as follows: no objection from any party to this

proceeding who responded to NMDOJ’s inquiry regarding consent (Walmart, FEW, SPS, LES,

Targa, CCAE, OPL, NMLGC). No response from EMNRD or Staff.

       4.      A copy of the proposed Statement of Position is attached hereto as Exhibit A.

WHEREFORE, for the reasons stated herein, NMDOJ respectfully requests the Commission to

allow it to file its Statement of Position out of time and for such other relief as is just and

reasonable.
                       Respectfully submitted,

